            "43: def is_glob_pattern(path: str) -> bool:",
            "44:     \"\"\"Return True when *path* contains glob metacharacters.",
            "45: ",
            "46:     A path with any of ``*``, ``?``, ``[``, or ``{`` is treated as a glob",
            "47:     pattern.  A plain literal path (e.g. ``src/foo/bar.py``) has none of",
            "48:     these characters.",
            "49:     \"\"\"",
            "50:     return any(c in path for c in (\"*\", \"?\", \"[\", \"{\"))",
            "51: ",
            "52: "
          ]
