          "lines": [
            "1: \"\"\"Lane computation algorithm.",
            "2: ",
            "3: Groups work packages into execution lanes using a union-find structure.",
            "4: Two WPs are placed in the same lane when:",
            "5: ",
            "6: 1. They have overlapping owned_files globs (write-scope conflict).",
            "7: 2. They share predicted surface tags and ownership is not provably disjoint.",
            "8: ",
            "9: Dependency edges do not collapse lanes by themselves. They are preserved as",
            "10: lane-level dependencies so disjoint upstream workstreams can run in parallel and",
            "11: fan-in WPs become the synchronization point.",
            "12: \"\"\"",
            "13: ",
            "14: from __future__ import annotations",
            "15: ",
            "16: from dataclasses import dataclass",
